{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S7 (aabf) Phase 4a recon complete. SCOPE FINDING: S7 is epic-sized. Deliverables: (1) NEW scripts/check_config_ownership.py (~500-LOC AST gate, mirrors check_config_reads.py contract) + approved-owner/seam registry; (2) NEW scripts/gen_config_reference.py + docs/security.md, regen docs/config.md (648L) from registry; (3) wire both ownership+field-consumption gates into make lint (currently only check_complexity_baseline is wired) + _build-and-test.yml + tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py (1190L); (4) NEW tests/scripts/test_check_config_ownership{,_heldout}.py red-proof fixtures; (5) CUTOVER: ~110 os.getenv/os.environ reads across ~70 files OUTSIDE config/provider seams must be cut-to-seam OR registered with exact path+symbol+rationale, exception set EMPTY before close, keeping all S1-S6 suites green. Sample calibration shows a MIX: genuine credential reads needing cutover (_cli/_jira_onboard.py JIRA_URL/USER/PROJECT/TOKEN; access_check.py), REBAR_* test/deterministic controls needing registry entries (hlc REBAR_HLC, lock REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES, usage_log REBAR_USAGE_LOG), and env-WRITES/subprocess-env construction that aren't reads (import_ndjson REBAR_SYNC_PUSH, git_fetch {**os.environ,GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT}). Realistically many hours + high build-churn risk; arguably its own epic (its plan lists 5 landable slices). Pausing to confirm approach with user: one large change vs decompose into slices."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787081343660524001,"uuid":"37909b92-a18f-42c8-a523-94c82c0ada2c"}